# J31 — Prove MODEL LADDER card: preview ≡ drafted command (P1 identity contract)
#
# Keyless, deterministic. The Prove `v` investigation card renders a MODEL LADDER
# (gate → panel → escalate) from the operator-stored verify:finding model knobs,
# and previews the exact `run verify:finding {…}` the Enter-to-draft handler
# drafts — one source of truth, so the preview can never diverge from what runs.
#
# Two branches in one isolated HOME, unset FIRST (no default is invented), then
# set (the drafted JSON carries the stored models verbatim). The card drafts but
# NEVER runs (Run Focus must not appear on the card's Enter).
#
# Width variants (operator matrix): re-run with `--size 60x20` — narrow Prove
# must keep identity/STATUS/NEXT before the ladder and never truncate a model
# name into ambiguity.
name: Prove MODEL LADDER card preview equals the drafted command
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 RUN FOCUS
keys: b
wait-for: 30 findings / 1 crit
wait: 2
submit: workbench
wait: 2
nav-mode:
keys: 4
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Prove | 1-prove
keys: v
wait-live-snap: 10 INVESTIGATE | 2-card-unset
expect: MODEL LADDER
expect: gate: not set
expect: escalate on tie: not set
ask: Unset branch — the ladder reads top-down as execution order (gate -> panel -> escalate); absence is meaningful (single-tier verification), not an invented default?
keys: Enter
wait: 2
snap: drafted-unset
expect-not: "gateModel"
expect-not: "escalationModel"
expect-not: ACTIVITY
ask: L2 guard — the drafted JSON OMITS gateModel/escalationModel when unset (no `gate: default` folded into the command); nothing ran (no Run Focus)?
keys: Escape
wait: 1
# setg writes for the focused tool, so focus verify:finding (via its options
# view) before storing the model knobs — then the ladder folds them in.
submit: options verify:finding
wait: 1
submit: setg gateModel openai:gpt-cheap
wait: 1
submit: setg escalationModel openai:gpt-strong
wait: 1
submit: workbench
wait: 2
nav-mode:
keys: 4
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Prove | prove-set
keys: v
wait-live-snap: 10 INVESTIGATE | 3-card-set
expect: MODEL LADDER
expect: gate: openai:gpt-cheap
expect: escalate on tie: openai:gpt-strong
ask: Does the hint teach `setg gateModel …` in place, and does the ladder read as the order of execution (gate -> panel -> escalate)?
keys: Enter
wait: 2
snap: drafted-set
# The composer shows the command's tail (cursor at end); serde sorts the JSON
# keys so gateModel + mode land in the visible tail, proving the stored model
# folded into the drafted command.
expect: "gateModel":"openai:gpt-cheap"
expect-not: ACTIVITY
ask: BYTE-IDENTITY (L1) — the card preview and the Enter-draft both come from the single source of truth `investigation_verify_command` (ui_view_models/phase_cockpit/confirm.rs), so they cannot diverge by construction. Confirm the drafted command carries the same gate/escalation models the ladder disclosed (the 68-char fingerprint makes the full JSON line wider than any terminal, so read the models from the ladder rows, not the truncated JSON tail).
ask: Nothing-runs invariant — the card drafted the command into the prompt; only a second prompt-Enter would run it (no Run Focus/ACTIVITY appeared).
